Z||000000||theogre||12-06-2000||08:41 PM||||A good number of you have seen me mention the AutoXray scanners. It's been awhile since I looked at their current product....<P>The version of scanner I have, the GM only version of the XP240 scanners is no longer made.<P>It is replaced by the EZ-Link GM OBD-I Scanner. (part # 10110) Like the older version it includes the scanner cable and manual for GM cars from 82-95. It list for 179 but if you shop it around you can likely find it for less.<P>My feeling of my older scanner is that it is still the sinlge most important tool I have for this car. I'd never try some of the experiments I've done without it. It's been very handy on more than a few ocasions when fixing things. ((Gee, am I really running hot or is the F'ing gauge lieing to me....))<P>------------------<BR>Lake Superior? Is that what I stepped in? Sorry.||||reg||6
